WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:01.920
 Doesn't it look delicious?

00:00:01.920 --> 00:00:03.150
It's amazing.

00:00:03.150 --> 00:00:05.340
Oh my God, who is
going to eat this?

00:00:05.340 --> 00:00:07.380
Me.

00:00:07.380 --> 00:00:10.320
We never look at the
past in a nostalgic way.

00:00:10.320 --> 00:00:12.210
We look at the past
in a critic way

00:00:12.210 --> 00:00:14.950
to get the best from the
past into the future.

00:00:14.950 --> 00:00:17.130
Taka, join me please.

00:00:17.130 --> 00:00:21.310
Here's my buddy, Taka, my
brother in my restaurant,

00:00:21.310 --> 00:00:23.490
Osteria Francescana.

00:00:23.490 --> 00:00:26.320
We are rated the best
restaurant in the world,

00:00:26.320 --> 00:00:28.080
but it's much more than that.

00:00:28.080 --> 00:00:31.740
It's about feeding
people with emotions.

00:00:31.740 --> 00:00:34.710
[SPEAKING ITALIAN]

00:00:34.710 --> 00:00:38.850
I want to teach you the way
to evolve classic recipes

00:00:38.850 --> 00:00:44.680
from traditional Italian cuisine
and bring them into the future.

00:00:44.680 --> 00:00:46.980
This is like the pasta
is talking to you,

00:00:46.980 --> 00:00:49.350
when it's saying eat me, please.

00:00:49.350 --> 00:00:49.920
Eat me.

00:00:49.920 --> 00:00:52.280
I am here for you.

00:00:52.280 --> 00:00:54.590
How you can improve
tradition-- this

00:00:54.590 --> 00:00:56.940
is panettone in a
traditional way.

00:00:56.940 --> 00:01:00.100
This is a panettone you
can make from the leftover.

00:01:00.100 --> 00:01:01.260
Can you imagine?

00:01:01.260 --> 00:01:03.760
But this is 100 times
better than this.

00:01:03.760 --> 00:01:05.519
You know, in cooking
you always have

00:01:05.519 --> 00:01:08.130
to keep the door open
for the unexpected.

00:01:08.130 --> 00:01:09.420
I want to tell you a story.

00:01:09.420 --> 00:01:13.700
At the moment I had to
create pesto for 120 people.

00:01:13.700 --> 00:01:14.850
We are out of pine nuts.

00:01:14.850 --> 00:01:16.020
What are we going to do?

00:01:16.020 --> 00:01:16.980
Bread crumbs.

00:01:16.980 --> 00:01:20.860
We put bread crumbs
instead of pine nuts.

00:01:20.860 --> 00:01:24.480
This is like, exactly how to
evolve tradition-- tradition

00:01:24.480 --> 00:01:25.950
in evolution.

00:01:25.950 --> 00:01:28.090
Don't throw away anything.

00:01:28.090 --> 00:01:31.440
You can use everything
and make it even better.

00:01:31.440 --> 00:01:34.170
Ask those ingredients
the right question.

00:01:34.170 --> 00:01:35.490
They're going to answer.

00:01:35.490 --> 00:01:39.000
Cooking is an act of love, and
it's bigger and it's deeper.

00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:41.717
So you, you're going to
explore where you come from.

00:01:41.717 --> 00:01:43.300
You're going to
explore your memories.

00:01:43.300 --> 00:01:45.150
Your palate is
going to talk to you

00:01:45.150 --> 00:01:48.480
and it's going to
tell you where to go.

00:01:48.480 --> 00:01:50.880
It's up to you because
you are expressing

00:01:50.880 --> 00:01:55.170
yourself, your experience,
your own flavor.

00:01:55.170 --> 00:01:59.770
I'm going to show you how
to be free to imagine,

00:01:59.770 --> 00:02:03.730
to dream, to transfer emotion.

00:02:03.730 --> 00:02:08.340
Sono Massimo Bottura
e questa e la mia MasterClass.

